@*
    The default mounting of NexusApiKeyManager. Same idea as SignInPage — replace or embed the
    component, this page is only the fallback.
*@
@page "/account/keys"
@namespace NexusSyncServer.Modules.Auth.Pages
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization

@* Anonymous visitors are sent to the provider picker rather than shown a page telling them to
   go there. The cookie handler already knows the way — AuthModule sets LoginPath — so this
   attribute is the whole redirect, and it comes back here afterwards via ReturnUrl.

   The component itself keeps its own signed-out message: embedded in somebody's own page,
   there is no guarantee the host page requires authentication. *@
@attribute [Authorize]

<PageTitle>API keys</PageTitle>

<NexusApiKeyManager />
